#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lommel_s2

#% text
# `lommel_s2(mu, nu, z)` gives the Lommel function `S_(mu, nu)(z)`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `S_(mu, nu)(z)` is the solution of the same equation as `lommel_s1` that behaves like `z^(mu - 1)` for large `z` (DLMF 11.9.5); it is `s_(mu, nu)(z)` plus a combination of `bessel_j` and `bessel_y`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lommel_s2(0.5, 0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 1.0000000000000002

#% cell
lommel_s2(1.5, 0.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 1.4142135623730951

#% cell
lommel_s2(0.5, 0.5, 50.0)
#% output
#= 0.1414213562373095

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# For large `z` it approaches `z^(mu - 1)`:

#% cell
lommel_s2(0.5, 0.25, 1000.0)*1000.0^0.5
#% output
#= 0.9999998125011601

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `lommel_s1`, `struve_h`, `bessel_y`
